# Docs voice (consumer)

Public MDX under `content/` is **AI-centric**: ViraUI is built so agents compose UI against a stable contract. **Humans** read these pages to decide, steer, and review that work — and to copy prompts. It is **not** a study guide where a person must memorize APIs, tokens, or prop inventories before shipping.

Contract: `specs/001-llm-first-docs-site/contracts/page-shell.md`.

## Voice split

| Page kind | Voice |
| --- | --- |
| Design System intro | Product-story |
| Get started / Foundation | How it works + prompt-first where required |
| Components | Task-oriented (when / when not / vs siblings) |

## Do

- Explain **how this ViraUI part works** and **when to reach for it** — speak to the reader with “you” when natural
- Default path: agent does the work; human reviews. Docs help when choosing or doubting
- Lead with copy-ready **configuration / compose prompts** on instructional and component pages (titled or tabbed fences); keep manual steps only when strictly necessary and secondary
- Write **prompt examples as consumer intents**: the result the person wants in plain language. Skills and published specs teach the agent the ViraUI mechanics — the pasted prompt should not require memorizing token names, prop APIs, package paths, or skill internals
- Prefer **short paragraphs** (about 2–3 in the lead before the next `##`) separated by blank lines — not one text wall
- Use **bullets, Callouts, and headings** when they make the idea easier to assimilate than a long paragraph (comparisons, when/when-not, checklists)
- Cross-link when another topic owns the detail; stay on this page’s job
- Em-dashes **rarely**, always with spaces when used: ` — `

## Do not

- Tutorialize as if the consumer must perform every step by hand (prefer prompt + how-it-works / when-to-use)
- Dump technical internals useless to a ViraUI consumer (package plumbing trivia, exhaustive prop dumps)
- Put ViraUI internals into **example prompts**: token names (`--duration-*`, `--global-*`), compound part APIs, `Read @viraui/react/specs…`, import-order recipes, or “Use viraui-design” openers — unless the page’s job is naming a skill (Skills) or wiring MCP tools (MCP)
- Habitual em-dashes or telegraph-style stacks of short sentences ending in periods
- Digress into other products or adjacent topics when a link would do
- Add “What’s next”, “Next steps”, or similar outbound tour sections
- Meta / editorial asides about the page itself: “Keep this page for…”, “This page covers…”, “not documented here”, “out of scope on this page”, “we only document…”, “without a catalog to maintain…”
- Talk to the author or agent about content boundaries inside consumer copy (put that in specs/contracts/rules)
- Authoring hygiene for the LLM inside consumer prose: “omit defaults”, “leave prop X off”, “examples stay honest”, “do not invent props”, “skills own the live set” — those belong in skills/rules, not MDX. Show the good shape in code; explain the mechanism in prose
- “Readers should…” / “Developers will…” when “you” or direct mechanism works
- Maintain surface catalogs of parts/tokens (see `.cursor/rules/03-docs-no-surface-catalog.mdc`)

## Examples

| Avoid | Prefer |
| --- | --- |
| Keep this page for ViraUI-custom helpers only. | These helpers are ViraUI-specific. The agent adds them when the app needs that behavior. |
| Follow these five manual steps to install… | Install the skills pack, reload the editor, then paste the setup prompt. Manual wiring stays below only if you must do it by hand. |
| One dense paragraph that lists every prop and sibling. | Short lead on the job of the part, then bullets for when to use / when not. |
| Short. Punchy. One idea each. | Connected sentences inside a short paragraph, or a tight bullet list — not a telegraph stack. |
| What’s next: Themes → Skills → … | Link Themes or Skills inline where the mechanism needs them. |
| Add hover with `--duration-fast` and `--easing-standard`; include `prefers-reduced-motion`. | Add a subtle hover animation on this custom card — not too fast — and respect reduced-motion settings. |
| Use viraui-design. Read @viraui/react/specs for Button… | Add a footer with Save, Cancel, and Delete — Save primary, Delete destructive, show loading on Save while it runs. |
| Omit every prop that matches the default so examples stay honest. | A bare Button is already primary; reach for another treatment when the action is not the commit. |
| …and pill shape without a prop catalog to maintain. | …optional addon, loading state, and pill shape. |
